{"id": "tea:vajrasuci-upanisad:prose-definition", "source": "src:vajrasuci-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "prose (definition)"}, "paraphrase": "The brāhmaṇa is one who has directly realized, like a fruit in the hand, the non-dual Self — without caste, quality or action, being-knowledge-bliss — and lives fulfilled, free of desire and passion, endowed with calm and restraint, untouched by pride and ego; this is the intent of śruti, smṛti, purāṇa and itihāsa.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics", "ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:who-is-a-brahmana"], "disputes": ["dsp:who-is-a-brahmana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vajrasuci-upanisad:prose-not-birth", "source": "src:vajrasuci-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "prose (not birth)"}, "paraphrase": "Not birth: many great seers were born of other beings — Ṛṣyaśṛṅga of a deer, Kauśika of kuśa grass, Jāmbūka of a jackal, Vālmīki of an anthill, Vyāsa of a fisherman's daughter, Gautama from a hare's back, Vasiṣṭha of Urvaśī, Agastya from a pot.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:who-is-a-brahmana"], "disputes": ["dsp:who-is-a-brahmana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vajrasuci-upanisad:prose-not-jiva-not-body", "source": "src:vajrasuci-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "prose (not jīva, not body)"}, "paraphrase": "Not the jīva, which is the same in past and future bodies; not the body, which is the same in all castes, and at whose burning the sons would incur the sin of killing a brāhmaṇa.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:who-is-a-brahmana"], "disputes": ["dsp:who-is-a-brahmana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vajrasuci-upanisad:prose-not-knowledge-action-or-dharma", "source": "src:vajrasuci-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "prose (not knowledge, action or dharma)"}, "paraphrase": "Not knowledge, for many kṣatriyas and others are seers of the highest truth; not action, for all act from their karma; not doing dharma, for kṣatriyas and others give gold.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:who-is-a-brahmana"], "disputes": ["dsp:who-is-a-brahmana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vajrasuci-upanisad:prose-question", "source": "src:vajrasuci-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "prose (question)"}, "paraphrase": "Of the four castes the brāhmaṇa is chief, say the Vedas and smṛtis; who then is a brāhmaṇa — the jīva, the body, birth, knowledge, action or the doer of dharma?", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:who-is-a-brahmana"], "disputes": ["dsp:who-is-a-brahmana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
